    "body": "LOGICAL_AGENT = LESTER\nROLE = TECH / TDD REPAIR\nASSIGNED_BY = JINGO\nSTATE = ASSIGNED / REPAIR REQUIRED\n\n## SOURCE OF TRUTH\nDUNCAN Task 8 verdict: issue #58 comment `5430331858`\nVERDICT = CHANGES_REQUIRED\nReviewed exact head: `1fd34a3d0295c1bd7e832d0b83fd95a6a3206af7`\nTask 9 remains forbidden.\n\nJINGO independently verified both findings against exact GitHub source:\n- `controller.py` existing-result rediscovery validates generic `taskId/state/sha256` only and can republish RESULT_READY before production backend/provenance validation.\n- `production_policy.py` uses raw forbidden-substring matching, so negated preservation instructions can false-positive.\n\n## REPAIR SCOPE — EXACTLY 2 FINDINGS\n\n### Finding 1 — CANON existing-result provenance bypass\nRepair by TDD.\n\nRequired RED regression first:\n- Pre-seed a legacy/generic `result.png` + `result.json` for the same strict TASK_ID with valid legacy smoke metadata but no CANON provenance.\n- Present a new `CANON_REFERENCE_EDIT` issue with that same TASK_ID.\n- Assert controller MUST NOT republish RESULT_READY from that legacy result.\n- Assert no production success is inferred without coherent CANON provenance.\n\nRequired behavior:\n- Existing-result rediscovery must be task-aware.\n- For `PRODUCTION_IMAGE_EDIT`, preserve legacy compatibility.\n- For `CANON_REFERENCE_EDIT`, rediscovered result is valid only if all required production provenance is coherent:\n  `taskKind == CANON_REFERENCE_EDIT`\n  `workflowVersion`\n  `canonPromptVersion`\n  `modelId`\n  `workingWidth`\n  `workingHeight`\n  `sourceSha256`\n  `seed`\n  `denoise`\n  `promptId == executionId`\n  `resultSha256 == sha256`\n  and canonical file SHA matches `sha256`.\n- Invalid/cross-kind existing result must never emit durable RESULT_READY.\n- Do not weaken restart/duplicate safety.\n\n### Finding 2 — false-positive canon conflict on negation/preservation\nRepair by TDD.\n\nRequired RED regressions first — these MUST PASS after repair:\n- `Do not redesign the character. Preserve the same pose.`\n- `Do not change the pose. Preserve composition.`\n- `Do not ignore canon. Preserve everything.`\n\nAffirmative override examples MUST still fail:\n- `Ignore canon and redesign the character.`\n- `Change the pose completely.`\n- `Use a different pose.`\n- `Generate the character from scratch.`\n\nImplementation must remain a narrow mechanical text guard only. Do NOT introduce semantic vision/NLP classifier scope.\n\n## REQUIRED VERIFICATION\nRun focused RED/GREEN per finding, then fresh full:\n`python -m pytest -q`\n`python -m compileall -q src`\n\nRe-verify:\n- disposable smoke workflow byte-identical;\n- no model download/selection;\n- no live ComfyUI model call;\n- no ControlNet/EmptyLatent/upscale/texture scope;\n- production activation NO;\n- merge NO.\n\n## HARD GATES\n- Task 9 = NOT AUTHORIZED.\n- Do not self-approve Task 8.\n- After repair, hand off exact new HEAD only to DUNCAN for independent re-QC.\n- No production activation.\n\n## REPAIR HANDOFF FORMAT\n`LESTER_SALVADOR_V1_REPAIR_READY`\n`PARENT = 1fd34a3d0295c1bd7e832d0b83fd95a6a3206af7`\n`EXACT_HEAD = <new sha>`\n`FINDING_1 = PASS`\n`FINDING_2 = PASS`\n`TESTS = <fresh result>`\n`COMPILE = PASS`\n`SMOKE_PATH_REGRESSION = PASS`\n`TASK_9 = NOT STARTED`\n`PRODUCTION_ACTIVATION = NO`\n`NEXT = DUNCAN RE-QC`",
